 \paragraph{IV 17.15.6--15.7, local and geometric descriptions (sites 162--164).}
 Number 15.6 writes a local description inside a regular locally noetherian ambient prescheme, using the stated regular sequence and the elementary singular zero of its defining functions. It then records the complete-intersection consequence and appeals to 15.4 for the reduction to one equation in a regular intermediate prescheme. The continuation on site 163 states the Cohen--Macaulay consequence and postpones the isolation assertion to a blow-up calculation in paragraph 20. The normality and reducedness thresholds and the zero-dimensional description are preserved as written. The zero-dimensional discussion has a handwritten replacement of ``dim'' by ``rang'', specifies the least exponent annihilating the maximal ideal, and continues on site 164 with the polynomial quotient over the ground field. Number 15.7 gives the corresponding geometric formulation, referring expressly to 15.6 and 15.5; it describes the value of the $n$th principal part in the degree-$n$ augmentation piece and the smoothness of the resulting form. Its residue-field terms bear overlapping corrections that remain doubtful. The author inserts a bracketed reminder that openness of the smoothness locus of a form was omitted from 15.1. The end of the argument discusses geometric normality and reducedness, the rational zero-dimensional case, and the classical description of a plane singularity with distinct tangents. The following parenthesis asks that the agreement of the absolute and relative notions at a rational point be stated already in 15.2 and discusses a separable residue extension, with the author's own reservation about the word ``finie''. The old canceled version of the opening of 15.7 survives between the new typed lines on site 163 and remains separately transcribed. See \href{https://grothendieck.umontpellier.fr/web/viewer.html?file=../25.pdf#page=163}{site 162}, \href{https://grothendieck.umontpellier.fr/web/viewer.html?file=../25.pdf#page=164}{site 163} and \href{https://grothendieck.umontpellier.fr/web/viewer.html?file=../25.pdf#page=165}{site 164}.
